Z||000000||ptswhite||12-13-2001||03:31 PM||||Just had my clutch slave and master cylindersreplaced on an '86 GT.  Driving to the shop the transmssion locked up just fine and pulled the car up hills with no problem (but I had to synchro shift without the clutch, since both cylinders were shot)<P>Now my wrench tells me the cylinders he installed are fine, but he had a rough time bleeding the system. He thinks he's got it properly bled, but now the clutch slips.  He thinks I needa new clutch?<P>I'm not so sure, since it seemed to tightly locked up on the way tohis shop.<P>Whaddyathink?||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||12-13-2001||04:02 PM||||Welcome to the forum.<P>How many miles are on your clutch?  Seems to me if it was fine when you drove it to the shop that the clutch would not be bad.  Maybe something is keeping it from completely disengaging?!?!  Sorry, not much help here I guess.  Have been having my own clutch problems.  Hope this somewhat helps ya out!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieromaster88sig.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000002||ptswhite||12-13-2001||07:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B>Welcome to the forum.<P>How many miles are on your clutch?  Seems to me if it was fine when you drove it to the shop that the clutch would not be bad.  Maybe something is keeping it from completely disengaging?!?!  Sorry, not much help here I guess.  Have been having my own clutch problems.  Hope this somewhat helps ya out!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It had about 6,000 miles on it when went to the shop.  I think it was fully engaged and no signs of slippage.  <P>The problem now is that it won't fully engage.  Could this somehow be related to the difficulty bleeding the system?<P>My wrench mentioned that for a while he thought it might have something to do with a "short throw" on the slave's rod.||||reg||2
